  "id": "cerebellar-nucleus",
  "term": "cerebellar nucleus",
  "definition": "A cerebellar nucleus is a group of neurons in the cerebellum, such as the deep cerebellar nucleus, that receives input related to movement. In the source, these neurons are described as getting signals from spinal motor pathways and issuing motor output whose function is reflected by their receptive fields.",
